  "content": {
    "id": "p58-q13",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to $f(x)=6\\sqrt{x}$ at the point where $x=9$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x-y+9=0$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(9)&=6\\sqrt{9}\\\\&=18\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=6\\left(\\frac12\\right)x^{-1/2}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}\\\\f'(9)&=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9}}\\\\&=1\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent passes through $(9,18)$ with gradient $1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-18&=1(x-9)\\\\y&=x+9\\\\x-y+9&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
